    "shebang_directive": "tree-sitter-c-sharp retains `shebang_directive` as a named kind, but normal .cs compilation units never emit it under the pinned grammar; kept as SkipWrapper so the hard depth gate is not blocked by an unreachable node.",
    "var_pattern": "tree-sitter-c-sharp@0.23.5 never emits `var_pattern` for surface `var` patterns: `var x` / `var (a,b)` parse as `declaration_pattern` with `implicit_type` due to the GLR conflict among `_reserved_identifier` / `implicit_type` / `var_pattern`; kept as SkipWrapper so the hard depth gate is not blocked by an unreachable grammar node."
